# Build context for apps/flowstarter-library/mcp-server/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the repository
# root's, and this build needs the opposite of what the root file wants: the
# root excludes `apps/flowstarter-library/**` entirely (the app's image wants
# only that workspace's package.json), while this image IS that workspace's
# MCP server. Rather than loosen the app's context for a directory it will
# never use, this build carries its own ignore file.
#
# Deny everything, then name the two things this image is made of: the MCP
# server's own sources, and the four catalog templates it serves. An allow-list
# is the right shape here — the context is two directories out of a monorepo,
# and anything that arrives by accident is either dead weight in a layer or a
# secret in an image.
*

!apps/flowstarter-library/mcp-server/package.json
!apps/flowstarter-library/mcp-server/package-lock.json
!apps/flowstarter-library/mcp-server/tsconfig.json
!apps/flowstarter-library/mcp-server/src/**

# The catalog, matching TEMPLATE_CATALOG in
# packages/agentic-codegen/src/workspace.ts and the `templates` stage of
# deploy/hetzner-staging/Dockerfile. demo-coach (editor dev fixture) and
# dorin-portfolio (legacy) are deliberately absent; the Dockerfile asserts
# both halves of that.
!apps/flowstarter-templates/creative-portfolio/**
!apps/flowstarter-templates/local-trade/**
!apps/flowstarter-templates/professional-services/**
!apps/flowstarter-templates/wellness-therapy/**

# ...but never a template's build output or installed dependencies. The image
# ships SOURCES: node_modules for a preview build comes from the app image's
# own baked template tree, and a stale dist/ would be shipped as if it were a
# template file by `scaffold_template`.
apps/flowstarter-templates/*/node_modules/**
apps/flowstarter-templates/*/.astro/**
apps/flowstarter-templates/*/dist/**

# Belt and braces. `*` above already excludes these, but they are the files
# whose accidental inclusion would matter most, and a future `!` line that
# widened the allow-list should not be able to sweep them in.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
.git
